WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.290
VERION does not currently operate an autonomous content factory.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.240
People write every quiz question. They review it before publication.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:13.508
AI support comes later. Rights checks and human review must be ready first.

00:00:13.608 --> 00:00:20.042
We plan to use responses to licensed-title quizzes, collected with notice and any required consent.

00:00:20.072 --> 00:00:24.472
We plan reports with aggregate data that does not identify people.

00:00:24.502 --> 00:00:28.785
Before expansion, check value, bias, consent, retention, and cross-border transfers.

00:00:28.885 --> 00:00:35.318
The first AI use case is drafting quiz questions for titles approved by rights holders.

00:00:35.348 --> 00:00:41.188
Each draft must include its sources, the expected correct answer, and notes for reviewers.

00:00:41.218 --> 00:00:46.658
The scope depends on permission and reliable sources. Unlimited generation is not promised.

00:00:46.758 --> 00:00:51.037
A person reviews rights, facts, expression, and translation before publication.

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:56.427
People record rejected drafts and every edit. The system never learns from them automatically.

00:00:56.457 --> 00:01:01.177
The release process should record who reviewed each item and what changed.

00:01:01.277 --> 00:01:06.433
After publication, the company can measure response, accuracy, completion, and abandonment trends.

00:01:06.463 --> 00:01:10.863
After human review, those trends can improve question difficulty and wording.

00:01:10.893 --> 00:01:16.173
These trends do not prove popularity. Read them with sample size and bias.

00:01:16.273 --> 00:01:21.233
Investment in computing comes after measuring demand, quality, cost, and privacy needs.

00:01:21.263 --> 00:01:26.793
The current plan does not fix a final GPU count or construction date.

00:01:26.823 --> 00:01:31.982
Each expansion must reduce a measured unit cost or improve reviewed quality.

00:01:32.082 --> 00:01:37.655
The company expects its advantage to combine licenses, response data, and review records.

00:01:37.685 --> 00:01:43.525
A general AI model is not a durable barrier. Competitors can use one too.

00:01:43.555 --> 00:01:48.710
The company must prove its data and operations before claiming an advantage.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:54.170
The company plans to use AI for drafting, not for unreviewed autonomous publication.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.499
People remain responsible for rights, facts, expression, translation, and release.

00:01:58.529 --> 00:02:03.235
Seed should prove quality, cost, processing time, and measured user value.
